A||||32||LEE498||3.1 BUILD
Z||000000||LEE498||05-15-99||10:53 PM||||Well, i've just finished putting together some of my short block.Everything went together fine,but the crank.There were a FEW places on the block that were hitting the crank.Nothing major, a drill and a file took care of the problem. The rods were just fine they cleared. Just thought i'd let you guy's know how the build up is coming along.<br>
Z||000001||Phil||05-16-99||04:27 AM||||just remember to change your flywheel/flex plate 2.8's are externally balanced and 3.1's are internal
Z||000002||Eric||05-16-99||07:57 AM||||Hey Lee, what's the part number on your pistons? Thanks.
Z||000003||Eric||05-16-99||07:59 AM||||Are you using a windage tray?
Z||000004||LEE498||05-16-99||01:01 PM|||| Phil, i had the hole rotating assemely balanced,they just cut off the weights and drilled some holes in my 2.8 flywheel,and shaved some weight off the rods.A balanced motor will rev a lot more freely and last a lot longer. Eric The part number for the RIGHT pistons to use is #H562P NOT #H561P. H561P's are for the aluminum heads,they have a deeper dish,which will give the cast heads a VERY low compression ratio.(thanks Shaun:)) No i'm not going to use an windage tray, i don't THINK it clear the crank.     
Z||000005||Phil||05-16-99||02:35 PM||||It was cheaper for me to get a flywheel out of a Beretta than to have my old one machined  at least that's what the guy at the balance place said. Also a .030 over bore puts you up to a 3.2 Litre - add a Melling cam, roller rockers ,port and polish and you will dyno at 215
Z||000006||LEE498||05-16-99||05:59 PM||||Hmmmm, 215hp sounds good! tell me more about this melling's cam.Is it better than the 2030 COMP? what's the lift? Is it STREETABLE? what's the power range? And who sell's it? Yes i know, i have an 3.2 i have an 0.40 over bore. The heads will be back in 2 week's i hope.You have any performance mod's done to your 3.2? did you notice a big difference in power-torque? I'm just curious, right now i only have about 120-140hp and on the juice 210-220 and it does damn good ,but having 215hp to start with then add the juice (90hp) phewwww! man i can't wait!! I might drop the juice down to 50hp to be a little safer.  
Z||000007||Phil||05-16-99||06:19 PM||||I'm building a Lambo clone so I'm still about 6 mo away from actually driving this thing but it idles ok. I'm too technically challanged to build my own engine today the last time I did anything like that was in the early '60 with a  Ford flathead(if you know what that is?) The rebuilder just said that he got 215 on his dyno but that is not in the car so it will be around 175-190? at the wheels
Z||000008||Eric||05-16-99||06:35 PM||||Thanks, Lee.
