Z||000030||Eric||05-20-99||09:43 PM||||All I know is the Crane Compu cam I found in the Jeg's catalog includes lifters in the kit.  The price is about $150 and also includes assembly lube.  The cam itself is milder than the Speed Pro, .423 intake .423 exaust with 264/274 degrees of duration.  This won't help you much, but I would try Summit for the lifters if you can't find them anywhere else.
Z||000031||Shaun41178||05-21-99||03:04 PM||||Lee you mentioned something in another post of perhaps revving your engine beyond 6k rpm.  Well if you still plan on doing that the stock lifters should be up for the job if you can find stock like ones.  <p>However I have a lifter here that might help more for prolonged high rpm use and will be better suited to do it.  They are reduced pump up types.  They are made by Johnson Industries but can be found in the Sealed Power Engine Catalog.  The lifter part number is HT2095  The price will probably be around $7 per lifter. which is around $84 for the complete set.  Hopefully you can get them cheaper then that through a speed shop or something or call summit and see if they have them or try Jegs too.<p>Also Lee who makes those rings you bought and where did you get them from? thanks
Z||000032||LEE498||05-21-99||09:40 PM||||Shaun, i got the rings from Advanace Auto they're the PREMIUM rings for the 93 lumina 3.1.Don't you just hate when you tell someone what you want and they ask ''why it's just a v6, it won't make any real power'' Thats what the machine shop guy said when i told him to put ARP rod bolts in my rods.If a customer is paying just do it, don't make any smart commets right!!Thats the way it should be.v6,slant6 or v8 it shouldn't matter. 
